{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 25, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "content": "Fair traveler thou seekest a journey to Japan's fair shores\nHerein lies an itinerary to guide thee on thy merry way\n\nDay the First\nArise thou early and take a flight to Tokyo's great city\nWhereupon thou shalt arrive in morn's earliest light\nTransfer to thy hotel and rest awhile from thy long flight\nThen forth thou shalt go to explore the city's wondrous might\nVisit the Tokyo Tower high and proud it doth stand\nAnd from its lofty height behold the city's grand design\n\nDay the Second\nRise thou early and take a train to Nikko's hallowed ground\nWhere thou shalt behold the temples of the Shinto gods renowned\nThe Toshogu Shrine a marvel of craftsmanship doth shine\nAnd in its beauty thou shalt be struck with awe and wonder divine\nReturn to Tokyo in the evening and dine on sushi fine\nAnd drink sake to toast thy journey's second day's sweet wine\n\nDay the Third\nArise thou early and take a flight to Kyoto's fair city\nWhere thou shalt behold the temples and gardens of a bygone era's pretty\nVisit the Fushimi Inari Shrine with its thousands of vermilion gates\nAnd in its grandeur thou shalt be struck with wonder at the gods' great states\nWalk thou the Philosopher's Path and behold the cherry blossoms' gentle hue\nAnd in their beauty thou shalt be struck with love anew\n\nDay the Fourth\nRise thou early and take a train to Osaka's bustling streets\nWhere thou shalt behold the city's food and drink in all its sweet treats\nVisit the Osaka Castle and behold its grandeur and might\nAnd in its beauty thou shalt be struck with wonder at the city's delight\nDine thou on okonomiyaki and drink sake to toast the day's sweet end\nAnd in the evening stroll thou through the city's lively streets to find\n\nDay the Fifth\nArise thou early and take a train to Hiroshima's peaceful shore\nWhere thou shalt behold the city's somber history and the atomic bomb's 